{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"OSEC-2026-26","published":"2026-10-23T21:30:00Z","modified":"2026-11-06T19:14:06.896521070Z","summary":"runtime_events user event name-based type confusion","details":"ANT-2026-DTBY2HWS \n\nCustom events maintains a cache of user events, it is possible to have a corrupt stream that has a valid message with one message type (which can be custom/unit/span/int) and then has the same event with a different message type.\n\nThis would never be encountered in a real program but can lead to a crash.\n\n## Fix\n\nValidate event type against expected type, report a corrupt stream on mismatch.\n\n## Am I affected?\n\nIf the runtime events producer and consumer run in separate processes, and the producer can be tricked into producing malformed data.\n\n## Timeline\n\n- 2026-08-24: vulnerability was found\n- 2026-08-27: forwarded report to security@ocaml.org\n- 2027-10-20: fix merged to trunk","affected":[{"package":{"name":"ocaml","ecosystem":"opam","purl":"pkg:opam/ocaml"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"5"},{"fixed":"5.5.2"}]}],"versions":["5.0.0","5.0.1","5.1.0","5.1.1","5.1.2","5.2.0","5.2.1","5.2.2","5.3.0","5.3.1","5.4.0","5.4.1","5.4.2","5.5.0","5.5.1"],"ecosystem_specific":{"affected_bindings":["Runtime_events.read_poll"],"opam_constraint":"ocaml {>= \"5\" & < \"5.5.2\"}"},"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/ocaml/security-advisories/blob/generated-osv/2026/OSEC-2026-26.json"}},{"ranges":[{"type":"GIT","repo":"https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"ac2fae847a9c2c35ae3bba90a19adbe5d0cc6f59"}]},{"type":"GIT","repo":"https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"de10a6b03a471821cb0b868223e5331b919f48c0"}]}],"versions":["flambda_fork_point","5.5.1","5.5.0","5.5.0-rc1","5.5.0-beta1","5.5.0-alpha3","5.5.0-alpha2","5.5.0-alpha1"],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/ocaml/security-advisories/blob/generated-osv/2026/OSEC-2026-26.json","vani